# `CLEAVE_LLVM_PREFIX` -- the LLVM 22 + MLIR + openmp install
# `cleave-mlir-shim`'s build script compiles its C++ against and links, and
# where `--run` and `cleave-build` find `libomp`.
#
# Run `scripts/setup-toolchain.ps1` from the repo root instead of setting it
# by hand: it downloads/caches the prebuilt toolchain `cleave-llvm-redist`
# publishes (`doc/building.md`'s fast path) and writes the real
# `.cargo/config.toml` (gitignored, machine-specific -- this file is only the
# tracked explanation). Already have your own LLVM/MLIR 22 build?
# `scripts/setup-toolchain.ps1 -ExistingPrefix C:\your\install` points at it,
# no download. Setting it some other way (a shell profile, a CI env step)
# works too:
#
# [env]
# CLEAVE_LLVM_PREFIX = "C:/path/to/llvm-mlir-22"
#
# `OPENBLAS_PREFIX` is a *different* case -- `cleave-rt` (`stdlib/blas/
# blas.cleave`'s own `Sgemm::sgemm`, the explicit, low-level BLAS entry
# point) loads `openblas.dll` explicitly at runtime, from a path baked in
# at compile time (its own default install location, `scripts/setup-
# openblas.ps1`'s own default `-CacheDir`, `target/openblas`) -- no link,
# no `PATH`, no env var needed for a plain `scripts/setup-openblas.ps1`
# run. Only set `OPENBLAS_PREFIX` here if you want to point at a different
# location, and only for a process cargo itself spawns (`cargo run`/`cargo
# test`) -- see `scripts/setup-openblas.ps1`'s own top comment.
